# M5 review (reviewer K): docs/design.md's "Every change to a present user
# entry is followed by its flush before the next user instruction", from
# ring 3 (user/root/src/tlb.rs). test=vspace checks mappings by walking the
# tables, never through the TLB. Thread T shares the root task's VSpace, so
# no CR3 write separates them and only each invocation's own flush can drop
# a translation already used. T reads a frame, the root unmaps it, and T's
# next read must fault; T writes it, the root remaps it read-only, and T's
# next write must fault; T reads a second frame, the root unmaps its page
# table, and T's next read must fault. After each fault the root maps the
# page back and the access restarts.
cmdline: test=tlb
exit: success
expect: microL4 kernel
expect: cmdline: "test=tlb"
expect: root: microL4 root task
expect: root: cmdline "test=tlb"
expect: tlb: T shares the root task's VSpace
expect: tlb: 1 T read F1
expect: tlb: 2 T's next read of 0x1000000 faulted
expect: tlb: 3 T wrote F1
expect: tlb: 4 T's next write to 0x1000000 faulted
expect: tlb: 5 T read F2
expect: tlb: 6 T's next read of 0x1200000 faulted
expect: TEST PASS
expect: DEBUG HALT 0 from TCB
